{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "gr-no",
  "connector": "の",
  "gloss": "’s, of",
  "title": "の — my, ’s, of",
  "pattern": "A の B (A’s B; a B about A)",
  "explanation": "の joins two nouns, and the first says whose the second is, or what kind: {私|わたし}の{本|ほん} — my book; {日本語|にほんご}の{先生|せんせい} — a Japanese teacher; {友達|ともだち}の{車|くるま} — a friend’s car. The order is the same as English ’s: the owner first.",
  "natural": "The second noun can go when it’s clear: これは{私|わたし}のです — this one’s mine.",
  "stiff": "い-adjectives don’t take の: {新|あたら}しい{本|ほん}, not {新|あたら}しいの{本|ほん}.",
